# Frontend — Angular Admin App

## Structure

```
frontend/src/app/
  core/           # Singleton services, guards, interceptors
  shared/         # Reusable components, directives, pipes
  features/       # Lazy-loaded feature modules per domain
    students/
    attendance/
    fees/
    institution/
    settings/
```

## Standalone Components

- All components standalone — no NgModules except routing convenience
- Lazy load features: `loadComponent` or `loadChildren`

## Required Patterns

```typescript
// Permission directive usage
<button *hasPermission="'students.profile.create'">Add Student</button>

// Route guard
{ path: 'students', canActivate: [AuthGuard, PermissionGuard], data: { permission: 'students.profile.read' } }
```

## HTTP Interceptors (order matters)

1. `CorrelationIdInterceptor`
2. `AuthInterceptor` — attach Bearer token
3. `TenantInterceptor` — attach `X-Tenant-Id` if needed
4. `ErrorInterceptor` — map ProblemDetails to toast
5. `TokenRefreshInterceptor` — refresh on 401

## Services

- One service per backend module: `StudentService`, `AttendanceService`
- Services call API only — no business logic
- Use signals or RxJS observables consistently (pick signals for new code in Angular 19)

## UI stack

- **Bootstrap 5** + **Bootstrap Icons** for layout, forms, tables, and components
- **Flatpickr** via `app-date-picker` — default date input for all forms
- **ngx-translate** — runtime i18n (`public/i18n/{en,ar,hi}.json`); language switcher in app shell
- **RTL** — Arabic sets `dir="rtl"` + Bootstrap RTL stylesheet; extend `LocaleService` for more locales
- Do not use Angular Material for new UI work

## AG Grid / data tables

- Use shared `DataTableWrapperComponent` for all list pages
- **Server-side mode:** `[serverSide]="true"`, `[totalCount]`, `(queryChange)` → API must return `{ items, totalCount, page, pageSize }`
- Client-side mode still supported for small/local datasets
- Standard column defs: actions column last, status as badge, dates via Flatpickr on forms

## Do NOT

- Store tokens in localStorage — use sessionStorage or httpOnly cookie pattern
- Hide buttons without backend permission enforcement (UI is UX only)
- Put API URLs hardcoded — use `EnvironmentConfigService`
